-- timers use the clock of the app (here a fake one)
at 0 ms: ticks 0, one shot 0
at 100 ms: ticks 1
at 250 ms: ticks 2, one shot 1
at 1250 ms: ticks 3 (a repeating timer that is late runs once), one shot 1 (only once)
cancelled: ticks 3
a timer cancelled before it was due: 3
more than 64 timers: the last id -1
-- the idle callback runs after events were handled
idle calls: 2
-- focus callbacks
Tab: 2 changes (lost + gained), focus on the button: 1
clicking the text field: 4 changes, focus on it: 1
-- shortcuts: with a modifier they come first, plain keys only when the focus does not want text
a bad key name: 0
shortcut 1
shortcut 2
typing x in the text field inserts it: 'ax', shortcut ''
with the button focused the plain shortcut runs: shortcut 3
shortcut 4
registering a key again replaces the action: shortcut 9, 4 registered
-- key hooks: the app hook sees every key first, a widget hook sees keys for that widget
F6 was taken by the hook: hook calls 1, shortcut calls 0
F4 passes through: hook calls 2, shortcut calls 1
the shortcut still wins over a widget hook (shortcuts come first): 'shortcut 7'
-- commands
1 commands, name 'Do it', keys 'Ctrl+J'
shortcut 7
